[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A RIPE Atlas probe only takes part in measurements once it is
registered with the RIPE NCC.

1. Enable and start the probe; on the first start it creates its key:

   sysrc ripe_atlas_enable=YES
   service ripe_atlas start

2. Register the probe with the public key
   %%PREFIX%%/etc/ripe-atlas/probe_key.pub at:

   https://atlas.ripe.net/register/swprobe

Keep the host clock in sync with ntpd or chronyd: the probe runs
unprivileged and cannot set the clock, and the controller rejects
uploads from a probe whose clock is off.

The probe logs to syslog with the tag ripe-atlas (facility daemon).
The measurement applets in %%PREFIX%%/libexec/ripe-atlas/measurement
are setuid root, executable by group ripe-atlas only: a small root
helper hands them raw sockets and BPF captures while the measurements
run as user ripe-atlas-measurement.
EOM
}
]
